+    // 25 s" is conclusive on its own. "Moved, but got no nearer" is not: it is
+    // also what a hard doorway looks like while the aircraft is still winning.
+    // Measured -- the run that mapped the most of this building spent about
+    // 300 s looping at (-10.5, -2.5), escaped unaided, and went on to 732.9 m3
+    // and every corner of the world; retiring its viewpoint at 25 s would have
+    // thrown that away, and the two runs that did retire early finished at 399
+    // and 479 m3 having never reached the south wing at all.
+    //
+    // So the looping test gets the longer window and the pinned test keeps its
+    // own. A moving aircraft still has options a pinned one does not, and the
+    // cost of waiting is bounded by the watchdog above it.
+    const double LOOP_WINDOW_S = 60.0;
+    const double PINNED_WINDOW_S = 25.0;
+    while (track.size() > 1 && track.front().first < now_s - LOOP_WINDOW_S)
       track.erase(track.begin());
     const bool at_target = (pos - next_pos).norm() < 0.6;
